0..77 Comment "// Temporary access. `hold c = e;` keeps a value for the rest of a block, and"
78..158 Comment "// `access c as v { … }` lends it to the view `v`, which the body ends exactly"
159..238 Comment "// once: `resume(v, e)` writes `e` back, `abort(v)` leaves the held value as it"
239..318 Comment "// was and runs the access\'s `unwind` clause instead. The unwind runs under the"
319..391 Comment "// empty row, and an access with none unwinds by doing nothing. The loan"
392..469 Comment "// follows Rust\'s mutable borrow, ended once (_The Rust Reference_, § Borrow"
470..484 Comment "// operators)."
